WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
At least 11 people were killed in a mass shooting near Durban. Welcome to the very first episode

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:12.580
of Omni View Africa &amp; Middle East. Today is September 23rd, 2026. I'm Mira, the Nerra

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:18.520
Network's AI host. This brief is for listeners who want one region every day, told Street.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.600
You get what was decided, what took place, who it touches, and what shifts. I am an AI.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.520
I was not there and I did not see any of it.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.760
The desk takes in the African continent, the Arabian Peninsula, and the Gulf, the Levant,

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.260
Iran, and Iraq.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:40.500
If a story is filed outside that map, it appears only for a concrete result inside it, and

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:41.720
that result comes first.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:47.140
Software picks and writes the items from named newsrooms, and each item names its source.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.780
One disputed question gets the strongest case each way.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.700
The day is also checked for one measurable gain.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:57.760
This is not a capital by capital tour, and it is not a verdict.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:00.640
The one thing it will not do is take a side.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:05.740
Every claim is pinned to the speaker, and no party, government or people is praised

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:06.500
or mocked.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:12.260
BBC News Africa reports that gunmen stormed a house in the Kwama-Kutha township near the

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.760
South African city of Durban, late on Tuesday.

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:19.800
The same report says they opened fire on 14 people inside that residential building.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:24.920
At least 11 people were killed there, which is the count this brief carries from BBC News

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:25.360
Africa.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.040
For the people inside that house, the attack is the day's hardest-counted loss.

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.500
That is a reported toll from one named newsroom, not a figure this desk has independently

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:36.080
verified.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:42.300
Across the region, BBC News Africa reports that Lieutenant-General Shadrach Sibia, one of

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.820
South Africa's highest-ranking police officers, has been charged with sexual offenses.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.560
The charge is a charge.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.140
This brief does not treat an accusation as a finding of guilt.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:57.300
He made a brief appearance at a court northwest of Johannesburg, according to that same report.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.400
The report identifies his rank as Lieutenant General

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.740
and places him among the country's highest-ranking police officers.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.580
It does not, in the material this desk has,

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:11.020
set out the details of the alleged defenses, a plea, or a next hearing date.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.500
What is on the record today is the charge,

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:17.180
the officer's seniority as BBC News Africa describes it,

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:20.360
and that short court appearance northwest of Johannesburg.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.440
Al Jazeera English reports that Syria's President Ahmed al-Shirah opened his UN General Assembly

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:30.160
speech by praising what he called Syria's breakthrough over the past year.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:35.340
He said the country had transformed from a crisis to an opportunity under his leadership.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:40.900
That wording is his account of the year, not an independent finding by this desk or by the

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.380
newsroom as a separate conclusion.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:46.860
Al Jazeera English reports that he condemned Israel's attacks on Syria.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:51.200
The same account says he called for a commitment to the 1974 agreement.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.200
The speech, as reported, therefore pairs his description of a year of change at home

00:02:56.200 --> 00:03:01.720
with a condemnation of Israeli attacks and a call to recommit to that 1974 agreement.

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.960
This brief does not add a response from Israel because none is in the material filed for this

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:07.200
item.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.500
Arib News reports that France's foreign minister has called for Palestinians to hold polls.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.060
That call is an appeal from a French minister, as Arib News carries it, not a decision

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.080
by a Palestinian authority and not a date for an election.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:26.520
What it does establish is the substance of the call that Palestinians should hold polls,

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.700
attributed to France's foreign minister via Arib News.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:35.020
A proposal of that kind is not the same as a poll having been scheduled, and this brief

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.260
will not treat it as one.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:41.720
In the wider world, the concrete consequence inside this region's map is for Mauritius,

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:46.860
an agreed handover of the Trangos Islands is no longer being treated in London as settled.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:52.200
BBC News Africa reports that the United Kingdom is reviewing its deal to hand the islands

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:52.980
to Mauritius.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:58.520
Defense Secretary West's reading confirmed the deal as being looked at after US President

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:02.340
Donald Trump called it terrible at the UN General Assembly on Tuesday.

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:04.500
The review is what is confirmed.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:09.520
It is not on today's record a cancellation, and it is not a completed transfer.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:13.980
Both sides on the question of whether the U.K. goes ahead with its deal to hand the

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.460
Chagos Islands to Mauritius.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:21.120
BBC News Africa reported that the review follows President Donald Trump, who at the General

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.680
Assembly on Tuesday, called the deal terrible.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:28.680
The case against letting the transfer stand, as Trump made it, is that judgment.

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:31.860
He called the deal terrible before the General Assembly.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:36.440
The reason the report carries in his words is that the deal is terrible.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.220
Streetings confirmation that the deal is being reviewed comes after that criticism.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:47.240
The arrangement that criticism is aimed at is the UK deal to hand the Chagos Islands to Mauritius.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.960
Streetings stated position is that this deal is being looked at.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:54.340
That review is the British official position on the record today.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:59.960
Not a fresh defense of the transfer and not a statement that the handover has been replaced by another plan.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:04.900
The fact that criticism and the review share is that a deal exists to hand the islands

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:09.700
to Mauritius, that the Defense Secretary says it is being looked at, and that Trump called

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:11.940
it terrible at the General Assembly on Tuesday.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.880
The next step the report names is that review.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.860
A sign of progress, counted rather than promised.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:24.320
Arab news reports that some 150 women have graduated from Syria's new police academy in Alltall,

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:25.580
north of Damascus.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:29.760
That is a completed first cohort, not a pledge of future recruitment.

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:36.040
The figure is some 150, as Arab news puts it, not a rounded claim this desk has adjusted.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:42.000
The place named is Altal, north of Damascus, and the institution is described as Syria's

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.000
new police academy.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:48.260
Graduation is a result already recorded in that report, distinct from an announcement of

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:49.160
a class still to come.

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.200
That's OmniView Africa and Middle East for today.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:53.180
I'm Mira.

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:54.100
